WEBVTT

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.900
Pauline-san doesn't seem to be anywhere.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.150
Where'd she go?

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.560
I hope she isn't caught up 
in some kind of trouble.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.410
Mavis-san, a letter's arrived for you.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.770
Thank you.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:20.650
No problem.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.720
Oh, it's from my younger older brother.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.420
"Younger older brother"?

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.460
I have three older brothers, you see.

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:32.840
I call them my elder older brother, middle
 older brother, and younger older brother.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.470
You do?

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.600
My brothers worry about me, 
so they send me letters every day.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.880
See?

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:44.360
Every day?

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.190
That's a little...

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.820
Well, they always write the same thing.

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.400
He's written saying to come home again.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.900
Is something wrong?

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.410
My younger older brother's getting married.

00:01:00.550 --> 00:01:02.890
Oh! Congratulations!

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.030
Is he marrying a noble?

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.590
The daughter of the Beckett Company...

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:10.210
Huh?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:11.860
Pauline?

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:15.010
What?

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.010
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:50.020
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:50.020
<b>No One Mentioned That Pauline's 
Getting Married, Did They?!</b>

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.240
Pauline!

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.150
Onee-chan!

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.900
Mother!

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:00.940
Alan!

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.410
Welcome back.

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:10.160
How was your Hunter training?

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:16.940
It's time for you to make 
yourself useful to us, Pauline.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:26.810
My family, the family of Count Austien,
 is a military family.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.470
As the kingdom's sword and shield,

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:32.690
we've won many battles.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.300
That's a distinguished family line.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.400
So why would someone from the military
nobility marry the daughter of a merchant?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.700
That's...

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:47.120
Waging war always requires money.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.790
As far as Count Austien is concerned, 
the more patrons the better.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:57.460
And we get that much closer 
to the royal family, you see?

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:01.040
Viscount Boardman!

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.060
Is that any way to look at your own parent?

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:06.890
Parent? What are you saying?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.010
As a count's family and a merchant's 
are a poor match for each other,

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:13.240
you will become my adopted daughter.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:17.770
As a viscount's daughter, 
Pauline Boardman, you will be married.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:21.110
Just how much do you plan to 
take advantage of my family?

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:25.380
What else do you expect? It is the 
reason I've kept all of you, after all.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.700
Do your best to be useful.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:32.090
It would be best not to 
turn your magic against me.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:32.860
Look.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:42.960
The reason I allowed you to go 
to the Hunter training school

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.560
was to increase your value as merchandise.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.550
That's right!

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.710
Thanks to that, I've found a good prospect.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:53.760
When they heard the bride would be able 
to use magic, they were overjoyed.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.060
Overjoyed!

00:04:55.540 --> 00:04:57.900
The count will be here very soon.

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.440
Be sure to behave yourself.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.650
Get it?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.250
This is Pauline-san's hometown?

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:16.500
It seems quite desolate.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.630
It's just like Lenny said.

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:24.520
They say that ever since that town got a 
new company head, it's changed completely.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.320
Please, be careful, okay?

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:32.400
That new company head was 
Pauline's father's enemy, right?

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:33.290
Yes.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:38.150
Pauline was probably forced to come 
back for a political marriage.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.860
I know I should be happy that my younger 
older brother's getting married,

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:45.900
but I don't want to do anything that 
would trample on Pauline's feelings.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.310
In that case, should we proceed with the 
intent of crushing this political marriage?

00:05:50.310 --> 00:05:51.210
No objections!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:51.950
Of course.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:55.580
Now that's settled, first, we need
 to gather information.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.340
It'd be nice if we could find 
someone who knows all about it.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:01.120
Hey! You there. Ladies!

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:02.880
This is your first time in this town, right?

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:07.510
That means you gotta pay the 
entrance fee and passage toll.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.400
If you don't have the money, we wouldn't 
mind you paying with your bodies.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:11.510
Pant, pant...

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.260
Another easy to read gang has appeared.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:18.610
We've been hired by this town's company head.

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:21.120
Go against him and things'll get rough.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.400
Pant, pant...

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.610
Someone who knows all about it!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:28.960
Um, if we stay here, everyone will see.
 That's embarrassing, so...

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.490
Could we go over there?

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.760
We're sorry!

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.620
We'd like to ask a few questions. Is that okay?

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:42.380
If you answer them nicely, 
we'll settle for only half-killing you.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.300
We're already half-dead.

00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:51.470
Tell us everything you know about your master,
 the company head that runs this town.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:55.100
Thank you for coming, Count Austien.

00:06:55.330 --> 00:07:00.520
Thank you so much for agreeing 
to marriage talks with us.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.160
We of the Beckett Company have,
 for a long time,

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:07.640
wished to pursue an amicable 
relationship with your lordship.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:09.060
<i>I could bring these two down at any time.</i>

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.460
Now that you're here,

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:11.830
<i>But then Mother and Alan would...</i>

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.490
I can assure you that you will be 
not only completely satisfied,

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.370
but overjoyed with this arrangement.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:14.370
<i>I have to find a way to help them get away.</i>

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:18.500
I've only come today to meet the bride.

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:20.930
Would it be the lady there?

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:22.740
Yes!

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:23.750
Introduce yourself.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:27.500
My name is Pauline.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:28.690
Right.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:32.220
Will you allow the two of us a 
little time to speak in private?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.290
Of course.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.560
Pauline, make sure you mind your manners.

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:44.420
U-Um, was there something you wanted from me?

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.830
"The Crimson Vow"... I think that was it.

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:48.480
What?

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:52.930
I know that you are a Hunter 
who works with my daughter.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.550
Count Austien...

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:58.060
So you <i>are</i> Mavis-san's father.

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.440
That's right. And...

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:04.080
I do not approve of Mavis being a Hunter.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:08.590
Perform your duties, and don't 
try anything uncalled for.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.840
This is a warning.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.180
Do you know about me, too?

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:18.350
My reach extends further than all of you think.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:19.940
Understand?

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:29.280
<i>I can't give up now,
after everything that's happened!</i>

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:33.500
Things are worse than I thought.

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:34.110
Yes...

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:39.310
Hoarding merchandise. Monopolies. 
Hiking prices unfairly.

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.800
Those who oppose him are sent to prison 
with no chance to defend themselves.

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:46.830
The company head here is exhausting 
every limit of evildoing.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:50.240
And since he's connected to the 
local lord, Viscount Boardman,

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.050
he can get away with whatever he wants.

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.520
Even setting Pauline-san's situation aside, 
this is unforgivable.

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.890
Let's go storm the place now!

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:57.930
Yes!

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.300
Calm down.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.520
We're up against a viscount this time.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.470
This is really bad.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:07.150
If we mess up, we'll all be fugitives.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.520
That's... not something we want.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.570
We wouldn't be able to work 
as the Crimson Vow anymore.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.460
We have to move carefully here.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:24.150
They just have to not know 
we're the Crimson Vow, right?

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:25.290
Well. I guess.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.620
Then leave it to me!

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:33.010
I feel like Mile-sama is trying to kill 
the seriousness of the situation again.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.230
A single flower blooming in the morning mist!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.320
Morning Dress Mask!

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.280
A single flower blooming in the sunlight!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.280
Afternoon Dress Mask!

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:59.240
A single flower blooming in the moonlight!

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.200
Evening Dress Mask!

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.500
Oh, dear. I knew it.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:06.700
We nailed it!

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:09.520
With these on, it won't matter 
if people see our faces!

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.720
Yes. That's Mile for you.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:15.350
Intruders!

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:16.720
Engage! Engage!

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:21.310
Oh! Oh no!

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:36.990
How many of you are there?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.630
I wonder what's happened.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:43.900
Pauline!

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:45.910
Mother!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:47.870
Where are the guards?

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:50.330
They went to help with the trouble outside.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.170
It appears something dreadful is happening.

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:54.540
I seized the opportunity and escaped.

00:10:55.020 --> 00:10:56.230
What about Alan?

00:10:56.230 --> 00:10:57.290
He's safe.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.930
I asked someone I could trust, 
who got him out of here.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.260
I'm so glad.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:06.060
I'm so sorry that I'm making
you go through all of this.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:11.010
Don't be. I made friends I can 
trust at the Hunter school.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.810
I was very happy.

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.900
I should be apologizing for not having 
fulfilled my duty as a daughter yet.

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:19.900
You... You couldn't be...

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.870
Oh! So this is where you are!

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.690
My lord viscount! She's over here!

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:28.250
Mother, you should hide.

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:32.850
What do you think you're doing here?

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.510
Sit quietly in your room.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:35.960
What's going on outside?

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:40.470
It's probably just some rabble from 
town who oppose the way we do things.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:43.600
Looks like we'll have to 
levy some more heavy taxes,

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.600
and show them who their masters are.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.210
Are you sure this is all right?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:54.150
Count Austien is here, yet you've 
caused an incident like this.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.270
It's nothing for you to worry about.

00:11:57.270 --> 00:12:01.220
Right now, the full military force of 
this mansion is out there cleaning it up.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:02.610
The full military force...

00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:05.990
Then there aren't any 
soldiers in here, are there?

00:12:06.210 --> 00:12:07.660
Of course not!

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.980
I see. Not one.

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.040
That means...

00:12:12.880 --> 00:12:15.670
Right now, I can bid the two 
of you a proper farewell.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.210
Ice Javelin!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.690
Don't do anything stupid!

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.960
Don't you care what happens to 
your mother and little brother?

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.180
Don't worry.

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:32.270
I'm right here.

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.960
What? Why are you here?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.270
What happened to the guards?

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.560
Mother!

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:38.730
Yes!

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.670
Don't come any closer!

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:44.610
This is revenge.

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:48.120
This is revenge.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.490
That voice...

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.500
Wh-What's this?

00:12:55.490 --> 00:12:57.630
This is for revenge!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.710
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.920
Who are you?

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.180
We are champions of justice! The Crimson Vow!

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.640
The Crimson Fountains of Blood!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:10.470
Hey! Why are you telling them our name?

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:12.260
Sorry, it just slipped out.

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:13.850
I wonder if they figured it out.

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:16.020
Crimson Fountains of Blood?

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.560
What an evil name for a party!

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:21.530
Thank goodness. We're okay.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.560
<i>They all came for me!</i>

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:26.620
What is all the commotion I've been hearing?

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:29.270
Count Austien!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.540
Th-This is...

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:33.980
This is revenge!

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:35.820
Two and a half years ago,

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:40.720
Viscount Boardman and the others here 
hired thieves to kill my father.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.550
They forged documents and 
took over the company.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.760
And now, they're committing every 
injustice imaginable against this town

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:48.540
in order to line their own pockets!

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:51.400
How dare you say such things?

00:13:51.400 --> 00:13:54.430
This girl seems to have 
taken leave of her senses.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:57.440
Please allow us to handle this matter.

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.940
My lord count! Please, listen to me!

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.190
I have heard both parties' arguments.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.900
There is no further need for words!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:14.880
Both sides should prove their 
righteousness with the sword!

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.500
Of course!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.910
What?

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:25.740
I am Pauline. To avenge my father, 
I am prepared to risk everything.

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:29.220
And to my friends who stand 
by me in my vengeance,

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:33.510
entrusting me with their lives 
and futures, I give my thanks.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:35.330
This girl!

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:38.270
I'll kill you before you can use your magic!

00:14:43.720 --> 00:14:45.040
What is this?

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:47.190
I'm sinking!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.360
Wh-When did you cast the spell?

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.240
Earlier, while I was praying.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.680
You don't have to say a 
spell aloud, you know.

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:58.960
You can just think it in your head.

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.330
Didn't you know that?

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:03.060
Y-You can use shadow casting?

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.090
That advanced technique where 
you don't chant the spell?

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:06.050
Yes!

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.240
Oh, I stopped.

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:14.930
Count your transgressions.

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:25.470
Mother...

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.680
Pauline... It's all over.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:29.320
Yes.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.810
My lord count, thank you very much.

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:36.700
With this, my late husband can rest easy.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:40.360
Gratitude is unnecessary. 
I knew of their evil deeds.

00:15:40.360 --> 00:15:43.420
This just happened to be a good 
opportunity to pass judgment on them.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:46.000
My true objective lies elsewhere.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.320
When I first heard of these marriage 
talks from Viscount Boardman,

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:54.760
and learned that you were the other 
party involved, I began planning.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:15:57.530
Meeting at the Hunter school...

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.640
The progress of the Crimson Vow...

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:01.330
Your bonds are strong.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:05.520
And for that very reason, you would not 
fail to rescue a friend in dire straits.

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.400
Isn't that right, Mavis?

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.360
I am a single flower blooming 
in the morning mist!

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:12.200
Morning—

00:16:12.590 --> 00:16:14.240
I am your father. You can't fool me.

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.890
To think someone could see 
through these perfect disguises.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:21.040
Is this the bond between parent and child?

00:16:21.550 --> 00:16:24.800
Thinking that these masks 
would work as a disguise...

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:27.750
You've all been completely Mile-sama-ified.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.380
You're coming home, Mavis.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:32.290
Father...

00:16:32.290 --> 00:16:36.520
Please, wait. Mavis-san is important 
to us as a teammate and a friend.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:38.280
Don't just take her away with you!

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.390
This is a family matter.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.820
You have no say in it.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:47.070
If you want to pretend to be a knight, 
I'll see you get some lessons.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.190
Come back home.

00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:49.770
Father...

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:52.990
No.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.610
The Crimson Vow is not a game.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.620
I want to become a true knight.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:03.310
You don't even know what a knight 
really is, and you say such things...

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.960
Teach her how a sword should be used.

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:06.880
Yes, sir!

00:17:07.210 --> 00:17:08.080
My lady!

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:09.090
Please forgive us.

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.500
Godspeed Sword! 1.2x speed!

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:15.510
What?

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.760
With this, I'm sure you understand.

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:21.940
The person I am now is not the person you knew.

00:17:21.940 --> 00:17:24.520
Everything is thanks to my master there.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:29.230
Me?

00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.350
She's your master?

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:32.980
That's right, Father!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.920
Interesting.

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.470
In that case, if she's stronger than me,

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:39.870
I'll let you have your way for a while.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:42.350
What? Father, does that mean...

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.050
How did things turn out like this?

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.340
I'm sorry, Mile!

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.140
Here I come!

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:56.420
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:17:56.980 --> 00:17:58.430
Your dad seems pretty strong...

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.910
It's because he's always going off to battle.

00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:05.020
My father's swordwork was forged on 
the battlefield, gained through real combat.

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.510
What's wrong? Is this all you've got?

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:13.270
Um, could I have a moment?

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.640
What is it?

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:17.210
It's a lot harder to move 
than I thought it would be.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.120
And it's hard to see.

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:22.240
Okay! Here I come!

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:23.910
What?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.550
Oh, you stopped me.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.750
Then I'll go faster.

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:34.490
<i>Her form is haphazard.</i>

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:38.010
<i>You can't call it swordwork, 
but she's got power and speed.</i>

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.150
<i>This strength... It's not human!</i>

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:42.050
<i>And yet!</i>

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:49.140
Whoever you are, you will return Mavis to me!

00:18:49.430 --> 00:18:51.870
Why do you go so far to oppose her?

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.310
Hunters can die at any moment!

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.030
You think I'd stand by and 
let Mavis become one of them?

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.910
I raised Mavis.

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.180
Dancing, singing,
playing musical instruments...

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.600
She learned every skill she 
would need to enter society.

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:08.070
I made her the perfect lady!

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.540
What does she have to be unhappy about?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.670
Mavis-san doesn't want any of that!

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:18.670
Whether she wants it or not, I have 
decided that it will make Mavis happy!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:21.430
That is an outdated way of thinking!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.140
I knew it. You are no ordinary girl.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:29.210
Are you a dwarf? A half-breed?

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:33.520
I'm just a normal, average human girl!

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.770
That's a lie!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:36.980
It's the truth!

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.350
End of match.

00:19:46.730 --> 00:19:48.450
A man does not go back on his word.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:49.730
She did it!

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:52.780
Father...

00:19:54.490 --> 00:19:58.360
For loving me, for taking care of me,

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.970
I thank you from the bottom of my heart.

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:03.840
But even so, I want to become a knight.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:07.720
A knight like you. No... 
A knight even greater than you.

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:09.330
So, please—

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:10.570
Miss Master.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:13.560
Huh? Oh, me?

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:16.770
Please take care of my daughter, Mavis.

00:20:17.140 --> 00:20:20.030
Oh, I'm still not much 
good at anything, but...

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:21.420
Father...

00:20:23.120 --> 00:20:24.780
Thank you!

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.330
Mavis!

00:20:28.570 --> 00:20:31.270
Guys! I'm looking forward to 
continuing to work together!

00:20:31.270 --> 00:20:34.210
Am I Mavis-san's guardian now?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:38.590
Well, I'll be off now.

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:40.640
Take care of yourself.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:42.420
Onee-chan, leave the company to me!

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.550
I'm counting on you, Alan.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:49.760
Work hard! You can do it!

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:54.770
Mavis...

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.860
Mavis!

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:05.470
Mavis! No, please don't go!

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:09.850
Mavis-san, your father really is chasing 
after us with everything he's got.

00:21:09.850 --> 00:21:11.950
The way you cry is exactly the same!

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.290
Driver, please make the cart go faster!

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:15.700
Wait!

00:21:17.880 --> 00:21:21.270
Don't you feel a little 
sorry for him, Mavis-san?

00:21:21.270 --> 00:21:24.830
He's fine. He did the same thing 
when I left for the Hunter school.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:26.790
So did my brothers. All of them together.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.070
I see.

00:21:28.570 --> 00:21:30.770
Pauline-san, are you sure 
you're okay with this?

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:33.850
You have to rebuild the company 
from scratch, don't you?

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:36.350
As long as my mother's there, 
everything will be fine.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:39.060
And my little brother is going to take over.

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:41.290
I know how it sounds coming from me,

00:21:41.290 --> 00:21:43.410
but isn't it lonely, 
being away from your family?

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:46.200
I can come back anytime.

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:52.710
And the Crimson Vow, all of you, 
to me you're already family.

00:21:56.860 --> 00:21:59.000
Thank you for coming to save me.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:03.360
W-We're family, so... you shouldn't 
just go off on your own!

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:05.350
Reina-san, you sure you should 
be the one saying that?

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:07.500
No one asked you!

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:12.890
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!
